      "name": "-heit",
      "description": "1. Converts an adjective into a noun and usually denotes an abstract quality of the adjectival root. It is often equivalent to the English suffixes -ness, -th, -ty, -dom:\n\t schön (“beautiful”) + -heit → Schönheit (“beauty”)\n\t neu (“new”) + -heit → Neuheit (“novelty”)\n2. Converts concrete nouns into abstract nouns:\n\t Kind (“child”) + -heit → Kindheit (“childhood”)\n\t Christ (“Christian”) + -heit → Christenheit (“Christendom”)\n",
      "source": "yomitan",
